WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.876
Good afternoon, my friends.

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:04.379
-Stillwater!
-Stillwater!

00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:06.923
Are you enjoying this beautiful day?

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.102
Hi there, everyone.

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:21.896
My name is Mallika Chopra.

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:25.233
I'm so happy we can spend some time
with each other today.

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:28.820
Together we're going to be noticing new things,

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:31.740
making some music,

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.203
- Nice song, everyone.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.539
- and even trying different ways of breathing.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.334
(Exhales)

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:49.716
And speaking of breathing, let's start by
just taking a big, deep breath

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:54.137
in through the nose 
and out through the mouth.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.388
In

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.515
(Inhales)

00:00:57.515 --> 00:00:59.434
and out.

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.019
(Exhales)

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:02.395
Breathe in

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.230
(Inhales)

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.815
and out.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:07.942
(Exhales)

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:10.904
Okay, I think we're almost ready.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:16.326
Before we begin, would you mind gathering
some things to help with this experience?

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:19.162
Can you find a comfy pillow,

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:21.623
a towel or exercise mat,

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:24.375
and a plastic bowl and spoon?

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:28.046
Feel free to ask a parent or adult for help.

00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:30.089
See you back here in about a minute.

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:32.509
Do you have any old blankets?

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:34.469
Have a look in the shed.

00:01:50.401 --> 00:01:51.945
Why, hello there. 

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:02.372
Welcome!
There's room for everyone.

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:30.233
Huh, there now.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.443
Have you found them?

00:02:32.735 --> 00:02:35.155
Great, this is going to be fun.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:39.951
Now take out your comfy pillow, 
sit on top of it, and let's begin.

00:02:53.089 --> 00:02:54.674
(Exhales)

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.009
Hello there.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:00.138
Welcome to a Mindful Moment 
with Stillwater.

00:03:01.472 --> 00:03:03.975
We are so glad you can join us.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:08.104
Did you know looking and listening 
to our surroundings

00:03:08.104 --> 00:03:10.607
can help relax and calm the mind?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.650
You might even discover something new.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.655
So today we're going to use 
our eyes to be mindful...

00:03:18.072 --> 00:03:20.491
and notice the world around us.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.249
There's so much color in nature.

00:03:28.249 --> 00:03:30.501
What colors do you see?

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:37.133
Green.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.802
Brown.

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:42.347
Blue.

00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:45.058
Red.

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:48.353
Grey.

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:51.272
Pink.

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:57.737
Ah, and look who added
one more color.

00:04:05.662 --> 00:04:08.289
Can you spot the red trees and bushes?

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:29.727
Look at the birds soaring
high above in the big blue sky.

00:04:38.903 --> 00:04:43.241
Do you see the ripples in 
Stillwater's Zen garden? 

00:04:53.918 --> 00:04:57.797
Or the rectangles on his house?

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.023
How about the rocks leading 
to his bridge?

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:24.449
And the arch shape as the 
bridge crosses the creek.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:38.129
Oh look, tiny footsteps in the snow.

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:41.382
Can you guess what animal it is?

00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:47.013
It looks like a small bird.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.228
Watch as the lanterns start to glow.

00:06:06.324 --> 00:06:09.952
And the fireflies love to glow too. 

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:19.962
Ah, the starry night sky. 

00:06:20.588 --> 00:06:23.424
Keep an eye out for shooting stars...

00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:26.803
and make a wish.

00:06:31.599 --> 00:06:33.559
Great job noticing today.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.354
So, how do you feel now?

00:06:36.354 --> 00:06:38.189
Actually, a lot better!

00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:43.903
I think it's wonderful you've come out here
to be so present in the world around you.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.738
Very good work!

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.240
Thank you, Stillwater. 

00:06:47.448 --> 00:06:48.950
I'm proud of you for trying.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.326
I'm proud of me, too.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.394
Hi, I'm Kishi Bashi.

00:07:16.394 --> 00:07:17.436
And I'm Toby!

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:18.813
Hope you like our music.

00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:21.482
K and I love to play music.

00:07:21.482 --> 00:07:24.610
We had a chance to write music for Stillwater, 
this wonderful show.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.279
Had so much fun.

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:29.532
It allows me and Toby, you know, 
the composers, to really

00:07:29.532 --> 00:07:31.033
to have fun with the music.

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:33.911
And we really would hope that
you would play some with us today.

00:07:33.911 --> 00:07:34.787
Would that be okay?

00:07:35.163 --> 00:07:36.581
Would you like to try?

00:07:37.081 --> 00:07:38.374
Uh, okay!

00:07:38.374 --> 00:07:40.251
We brought our instruments.

00:07:40.251 --> 00:07:41.210
Got mine!

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:42.420
Did you guys bring yours? 

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.255
Do you guys have your bowls and spoons?

00:07:44.547 --> 00:07:46.257
Toby, what do you think, 
are they ready?

00:07:46.257 --> 00:07:47.925
Let me see...

00:07:47.925 --> 00:07:50.428
yeah, they, I don't know, oh yeah, yeah, 
 they got them.

00:07:50.428 --> 00:07:52.388
Okay, so, let's make music together.

00:07:52.388 --> 00:07:52.930
Toby you ready?

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:53.723
I'm ready.

00:07:53.723 --> 00:07:55.183
Okay, well let's start with a beat.

00:07:55.349 --> 00:07:56.058
Okay, so,

00:07:57.268 --> 00:07:58.978
you guys grab your bowl and spoon,

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.313
(Claps)

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:01.230
And tap along.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.525
And it's okay if you don't have one, 
you can also just clap like me, okay?

00:08:05.193 --> 00:08:07.320
So clap along because I'm going 
to start playing the violin.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.070
Ready?

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.113
Great job, everybody!

00:08:09.113 --> 00:08:10.656
One, two, three, four.

00:08:55.326 --> 00:08:57.370
-Woo, that was fun!
-That sounded awesome.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.287
Great job.

00:08:58.287 --> 00:08:59.789
Wow,  you guys did amazing.

00:08:59.789 --> 00:09:01.040
You guys are all musicians here.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.667
Now I have a question. 

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:03.960
How did that make you feel?

00:09:04.335 --> 00:09:05.419
Happy?

00:09:05.419 --> 00:09:06.462
Calm?

00:09:06.462 --> 00:09:07.588
Excited?

00:09:07.588 --> 00:09:08.965
Sad?

00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:11.217
Music can make us feel lots of things.

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:13.803
The type of music that I really 
enjoy sometimes

00:09:13.803 --> 00:09:16.597
is music that just invites you to feel.

00:09:16.597 --> 00:09:19.475
It just, is this open invitation to

00:09:19.475 --> 00:09:20.810
experience something.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.728
I was about seven years old when
I started the violin

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:25.398
and I think I love it so much
because it's like singing.

00:09:25.648 --> 00:09:27.775
You know it's like na-da-da.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:34.699
And it's kind of like, uh,

00:09:34.699 --> 00:09:36.909
it feels really beautiful to me, 
so I've played it ever since.

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:39.704
K and I actually went to school together.

00:09:39.704 --> 00:09:42.081
So we were growing up playing
music together.

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:44.917
Playing music with your friend is probably
one of the best things you could ever do.

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:48.421
There's like one thing better than making music
is making music with your friends,

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:49.839
and that's so much fun.

00:09:50.047 --> 00:09:51.424
Hey Toby, why don't we play a game?

00:09:51.716 --> 00:09:53.217
Sure, what are you thinking?

00:09:53.634 --> 00:09:55.219
Let's try to name a feeling

00:09:55.219 --> 00:09:57.138
and then make music to match it.

00:09:57.388 --> 00:09:58.597
Interesting.

00:09:58.597 --> 00:10:00.308
Okay, let's give it a try.

00:10:00.725 --> 00:10:02.768
All right, well let's start with the 
feeling of happiness.

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:03.978
You ready?

00:10:03.978 --> 00:10:05.187
I'm ready, let's do it.

00:10:06.063 --> 00:10:07.606
You know, Toby, why don't you kick it off.

00:10:07.606 --> 00:10:09.275
One, two, three, four.

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:40.681
I'm pretty happy.

00:10:40.681 --> 00:10:42.516
That melody really made me happy.

00:10:42.516 --> 00:10:43.809
Toby, what makes you happy about that?

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.561
Yeah, the melody made me happy,

00:10:45.561 --> 00:10:46.687
and...

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.856
the ukulele always makes me happy.

00:10:48.856 --> 00:10:50.608
I like, the ukulele makes me happy too.

00:10:50.608 --> 00:10:53.611
Ukulele's such a cute little,
cute little instrument.

00:10:53.611 --> 00:10:54.570
I love it.

00:10:55.279 --> 00:10:56.614
Should we try the opposite? 

00:10:56.614 --> 00:10:57.740
Sadness?

00:10:58.282 --> 00:10:59.241
Let's do it.

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:01.744
All right, K. 
Sadness, here we go.

00:11:50.668 --> 00:11:52.128
You guys hear the difference?

00:11:52.753 --> 00:11:54.004
Quite different from happiness.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.297
It's a little bit slower

00:11:55.631 --> 00:11:57.550
And there's some sad chords 
in there too, right?

00:11:58.259 --> 00:11:59.468
Yeah, absolutely.

00:11:59.468 --> 00:12:01.512
You know, sometimes 
it's totally fine to be sad.

00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:03.556
It's just, that's what we do 
as human beings.

00:12:03.931 --> 00:12:05.933
If we don't have sadness, 
how do we know we're happy? 

00:12:05.933 --> 00:12:06.434
Right?

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:10.187
Every feeling you have
is just as important as the other.

00:12:10.187 --> 00:12:14.483
So, it's okay to feel 
any of those feelings.

00:12:14.817 --> 00:12:16.444
I've got an idea for the next one.

00:12:16.444 --> 00:12:18.112
How about excitement?

00:12:18.362 --> 00:12:19.655
I need some excitement.

00:12:19.947 --> 00:12:21.282
-Good idea, let's try that.
-Let's do it.

00:12:40.759 --> 00:12:41.802
That was pretty exciting.

00:12:42.303 --> 00:12:43.929
That's how excitement should feel.

00:12:44.096 --> 00:12:47.266
Sometimes excitement is hard because, 
uh, it's really fast.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.685
So you have to kind of keep up
with the music.

00:12:49.685 --> 00:12:50.936
So you're kind of running
along with it.

00:12:50.936 --> 00:12:52.730
That's a big challenge for me.

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.440
I almost drop my instrument sometimes

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:55.483
by excitement.

00:12:55.483 --> 00:12:57.902
I have dropped my instrument sometimes
from excitement.

00:12:57.902 --> 00:13:01.071
So, that's the danger of being 
too excited about playing.

00:13:01.238 --> 00:13:01.906
Yeah.

00:13:02.114 --> 00:13:05.034
So, for our last one, 
how about if we try calmness?

00:13:05.159 --> 00:13:06.494
Okay, that'd be a good one.

00:13:06.494 --> 00:13:08.454
Yeah, I need to calm down here.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.213
That was a lot of fun.

00:13:59.588 --> 00:14:00.923
I felt really calm.

00:14:01.048 --> 00:14:03.092
What about the music made
you feel calm?

00:14:03.259 --> 00:14:05.511
It was like long and soft.

00:14:05.928 --> 00:14:07.555
Nothing changed very quickly.

00:14:07.555 --> 00:14:09.098
It was very slow and smooth.

00:14:09.098 --> 00:14:09.807
Yes!

00:14:09.807 --> 00:14:10.349
Yeah.

00:14:10.349 --> 00:14:13.727
It took its time, 
and there wasn't a big beat.

00:14:14.353 --> 00:14:16.689
And, uh, it kind of flowed.

00:14:16.689 --> 00:14:17.523
Uh...

00:14:18.691 --> 00:14:20.359
Do you hear that sound?

00:14:20.359 --> 00:14:21.068
Is that you, Toby?

00:14:21.068 --> 00:14:22.027
It's not me!

00:14:22.486 --> 00:14:24.488
Wonder where it's coming from.

00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:25.906
Maybe you guys should go
take a look.

00:14:25.906 --> 00:14:27.700
Yeah, go check it out, 
let's see what that is?

00:14:27.866 --> 00:14:29.493
Thank you guys so much 
for joining us.

00:14:29.493 --> 00:14:30.160
This was great.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:30.869
We had a lot of fun.

00:14:31.161 --> 00:14:32.913
-Bye!
-Bye!

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.132
It is time for me to scoop leaves.

00:14:43.757 --> 00:14:44.717
Would you like to help?

00:14:44.842 --> 00:14:45.426
Sure.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:47.720
I like a clean pond.

00:14:49.179 --> 00:14:50.389
And so do the fish.

00:15:11.702 --> 00:15:12.411
Hey there!

00:15:12.745 --> 00:15:14.038
My name is Jessica Skye

00:15:14.038 --> 00:15:16.707
and I'm super excited for what we have planned today.

00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:18.667
But first,

00:15:18.667 --> 00:15:19.835
let's pause for a second.

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:21.962
Can you hear my wind chimes?

00:15:30.554 --> 00:15:32.306
I love listening to that sound.

00:15:32.473 --> 00:15:35.142
It always makes me feel so happy and calm.

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:38.228
And so many interesting things can happen when we just

00:15:38.228 --> 00:15:40.898
pay attention to what's happening around us.

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:42.775
And inside us.

00:15:43.442 --> 00:15:44.318
Like with our breath.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.278
Let's try it together.

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:49.531
Remember that mat or towel you grabbed earlier?

00:15:50.032 --> 00:15:51.700
It's time to roll it out on the floor.

00:15:53.077 --> 00:15:55.287
Feel free to move your pillow

00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:56.121
if you need to.

00:16:00.292 --> 00:16:02.252
And it's fine if you don't have a mat or towel.

00:16:02.586 --> 00:16:04.171
Just find a safe

00:16:04.171 --> 00:16:05.297
flat surface.

00:16:06.298 --> 00:16:08.425
Now have a seat and get comfortable.

00:16:09.176 --> 00:16:13.013
We're going to take three, nice, long breaths.

00:16:13.681 --> 00:16:14.848
In through the nose

00:16:15.599 --> 00:16:17.142
and out through the mouth.

00:16:17.643 --> 00:16:19.561
(Inhale)

00:16:21.855 --> 00:16:24.149
(Exhale)

00:16:25.317 --> 00:16:26.777
Two more and do it with me.

00:16:27.236 --> 00:16:27.986
Inhaling.

00:16:27.986 --> 00:16:30.447
(Inhale)

00:16:31.198 --> 00:16:32.866
Exhaling.

00:16:32.866 --> 00:16:35.119
(Exhale)

00:16:36.745 --> 00:16:37.496
Last one.

00:16:37.871 --> 00:16:39.623
Deep breath in through your nose.

00:16:39.623 --> 00:16:41.875
(Inhale)

00:16:42.418 --> 00:16:44.503
Heavy exhale through your mouth.

00:16:45.045 --> 00:16:47.297
(Exhale)

00:16:47.798 --> 00:16:49.174
What are you doing?

00:16:49.383 --> 00:16:52.886
Stillwater says "if you have an angry feeling inside you..."

00:16:53.262 --> 00:16:54.471
"...sit still...

00:16:54.471 --> 00:16:55.973
"...close your eyes..."

00:16:55.973 --> 00:16:58.517
"...and take deep, slow breaths."

00:16:59.184 --> 00:17:00.310
(Inhale)

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:01.437
(Exhale)

00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:03.021
It can make you feel better.

00:17:04.189 --> 00:17:05.023
Great job.

00:17:05.774 --> 00:17:07.568
Now breathing

00:17:07.568 --> 00:17:10.571
is one of those things that we do all the time.

00:17:10.988 --> 00:17:13.073
And sometimes we don't even notice it.

00:17:13.991 --> 00:17:14.616
But,

00:17:15.159 --> 00:17:17.828
if you're not feeling great on the inside.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:21.331
Taking a moment to catch a breath can change that

00:17:21.331 --> 00:17:24.251
and really help you feel calm.

00:17:24.251 --> 00:17:25.544
Is it working?

00:17:26.253 --> 00:17:28.172
Actually, it is.

00:17:28.797 --> 00:17:30.215
(Exhale)

00:17:30.716 --> 00:17:32.176
You ready to try something new?

00:17:33.343 --> 00:17:34.470
It's called

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:36.430
deep belly breathing.

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:39.391
And it's one of Stillwater's favorites.

00:17:39.767 --> 00:17:41.518
I like your big belly!

00:17:42.352 --> 00:17:43.312
Me too!

00:17:43.645 --> 00:17:45.898
I'd like you to put one hand right here.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:47.399
On the top of your stomach.

00:17:47.566 --> 00:17:49.026
Just below your ribs.

00:17:49.777 --> 00:17:50.861
And when you breath in

00:17:51.528 --> 00:17:52.738
do it through your nose.

00:17:53.405 --> 00:17:56.617
And I want you to try and make your belly big

00:17:56.617 --> 00:17:57.910
and full.

00:17:58.452 --> 00:17:59.620
It's like

00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:02.331
a balloon and we're filling it up with air.

00:18:02.998 --> 00:18:04.041
And when it's full

00:18:04.708 --> 00:18:05.334
go ahead

00:18:05.918 --> 00:18:07.878
and exhale super slowly

00:18:08.212 --> 00:18:09.505
through your mouth.

00:18:10.005 --> 00:18:12.090
Let me show you and then let's do it together.

00:18:13.258 --> 00:18:14.718
(Inhale)

00:18:17.221 --> 00:18:19.306
(Exhale)

00:18:21.183 --> 00:18:21.809
Ready?

00:18:22.017 --> 00:18:23.268
Do this one with me.

00:18:23.769 --> 00:18:25.521
(Inhale)

00:18:28.732 --> 00:18:30.984
(Exhale)

00:18:33.737 --> 00:18:34.696
Feels good, right?

00:18:35.531 --> 00:18:38.075
Let's do it a few more times together.

00:18:38.075 --> 00:18:39.284
Just keep going.

00:18:40.494 --> 00:18:42.287
(Inhale)

00:18:44.414 --> 00:18:46.667
(Exhale)

00:18:47.417 --> 00:18:48.836
Super calming.

00:18:48.836 --> 00:18:49.503
One more.

00:18:49.503 --> 00:18:51.755
(Inhale)

00:18:54.258 --> 00:18:56.510
(Exhale)

00:18:59.012 --> 00:19:00.556
Nice job filling up that balloon.

00:19:00.722 --> 00:19:03.892
Very nice! I think you're a natural!

00:19:03.892 --> 00:19:04.768
Next,

00:19:04.768 --> 00:19:06.353
I'd like to ask

00:19:06.353 --> 00:19:09.147
what are some of the things you notice

00:19:09.147 --> 00:19:11.692
when everything's super quiet?

00:19:11.984 --> 00:19:16.029
There are many different ways to 
be mindful in the world around you.

00:19:16.822 --> 00:19:19.157
Let's sit for a moment and

00:19:19.157 --> 00:19:20.075
just listen.

00:19:20.909 --> 00:19:23.453
And I find sometimes it helps me focus

00:19:23.996 --> 00:19:25.581
if I close my eyes.

00:19:26.331 --> 00:19:27.249
So give it a go.

00:19:28.292 --> 00:19:30.711
Soften your gaze or completely close your eyes.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.590
And just tune in with all those noises around you.

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:45.976
I can hear the water trickling behind me.

00:19:49.771 --> 00:19:53.066
I can hear the birds chirping in the distance.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:01.033
And the leaves rustling in the wind.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.748
What can you hear?

00:20:10.375 --> 00:20:11.793
Maybe there's a fan

00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:14.338
blowing air in the background?

00:20:16.506 --> 00:20:17.841
A car outside?

00:20:20.302 --> 00:20:23.388
Maybe your family are in the 
other room and you can hear them.

00:20:25.849 --> 00:20:27.142
So take a moment

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:32.856
notice if you can hear your own breath.

00:20:34.942 --> 00:20:37.194
(Inhale)

00:20:38.278 --> 00:20:40.530
(Exhale)

00:20:41.365 --> 00:20:42.491
Isn't it wonderful?

00:20:43.742 --> 00:20:44.493
Now let's

00:20:44.493 --> 00:20:46.495
use our eyes this time.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:47.704
How do we start?

00:20:48.288 --> 00:20:49.247
First

00:20:49.247 --> 00:20:50.958
start with what you see.

00:20:51.333 --> 00:20:52.751
The shape of the fruit.

00:20:53.001 --> 00:20:53.961
The colors.

00:20:54.503 --> 00:20:55.629
So have a look around.

00:20:58.382 --> 00:20:59.591
I can see...

00:21:00.425 --> 00:21:01.718
...pink flowers.

00:21:03.679 --> 00:21:06.390
I can see green leaves starting to turn yellow.

00:21:11.812 --> 00:21:13.146
I can see a red table.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:17.567
What colors can you find around you

00:21:17.567 --> 00:21:18.694
in your space?

00:21:24.741 --> 00:21:26.034
What color are the walls?

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:31.873
Maybe there's an object on a desk or a table?

00:21:32.541 --> 00:21:33.792
What color is that?

00:21:35.335 --> 00:21:37.838
Maybe even look outside your window.

00:21:38.338 --> 00:21:39.840
Notice what you can see there.

00:21:40.716 --> 00:21:43.468
There are so many colors in the world.

00:21:43.927 --> 00:21:45.178
So take a moment

00:21:45.887 --> 00:21:47.097
taking them all in.

00:21:55.188 --> 00:21:57.149
Excellent job using your senses.

00:21:58.025 --> 00:22:00.068
Now let's move on to something new.

00:22:00.402 --> 00:22:02.821
Go ahead and stand up on your mat or towel.

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:04.656
Just like this.

00:22:05.323 --> 00:22:07.117
If you got shoes and sock on

00:22:07.701 --> 00:22:09.578
go ahead and take them off now.

00:22:10.412 --> 00:22:12.581
We're going to give our toes 
something to do.

00:22:13.582 --> 00:22:14.708
All set?

00:22:15.042 --> 00:22:16.877
Let's scrunch our toes up.

00:22:17.336 --> 00:22:20.088
And notice what we feel.

00:22:22.466 --> 00:22:23.592
I can feel

00:22:24.051 --> 00:22:25.719
tingles in the tips of my toes.

00:22:26.762 --> 00:22:28.764
What can you feel beneath your toes?

00:22:29.181 --> 00:22:30.724
Is it soft?

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:35.479
Is anything bunching up between
you toes?

00:22:36.063 --> 00:22:38.106
Maybe you're on wooden floors.

00:22:38.482 --> 00:22:39.483
Or tile.

00:22:40.192 --> 00:22:41.401
Is it cool?

00:22:41.610 --> 00:22:43.028
Is it warm?

00:22:43.945 --> 00:22:46.239
Now let's move up from our feet

00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:47.949
to the rest of our body.

00:22:47.949 --> 00:22:50.202
Do you feel the air around you?

00:22:50.744 --> 00:22:53.580
Maybe there's a fan or a heater

00:22:54.164 --> 00:22:56.708
and you can feel it blowing air
onto your skin.

00:22:57.292 --> 00:23:00.837
Or maybe you stood near an open window
and you can feel the breeze coming in.

00:23:01.004 --> 00:23:03.590
Did you feel the cold on your back?

00:23:03.590 --> 00:23:05.175
That's my favorite part.

00:23:05.175 --> 00:23:09.179
Perhaps the air in your room is still.

00:23:10.138 --> 00:23:13.016
Try moving your arms slowly around you.

00:23:16.812 --> 00:23:18.230
I bet you can feel the air now.

00:23:18.230 --> 00:23:21.691
Just notice how that feels.

00:23:22.275 --> 00:23:24.569
It's like the air is moving out of your way.

00:23:26.822 --> 00:23:29.699
Just like ripples in a pond.

00:23:31.409 --> 00:23:33.829
All right, let's do one more type of breathing,

00:23:33.829 --> 00:23:35.080
and this is a fun one.

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:36.998
It's called "Bee Breath."

00:23:37.165 --> 00:23:39.084
That does sound like fun.

00:23:39.084 --> 00:23:41.795
You know how bees make a buzzing sound?

00:23:42.462 --> 00:23:45.215
That's where this breathing gets
its name from.

00:23:45.674 --> 00:23:47.884
We're going to buzz together like 
little bees.

00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:50.887
So let's take a slow breath in

00:23:50.887 --> 00:23:52.389
through our nose,

00:23:52.639 --> 00:23:56.184
and then this time, 
exhale with the mouth closed,

00:23:56.184 --> 00:23:57.769
and make a humming sound.

00:23:57.769 --> 00:23:59.062
Let me show you first.

00:23:59.813 --> 00:24:01.106
(Inhales)

00:24:02.858 --> 00:24:06.611
(Humming)

00:24:10.574 --> 00:24:11.992
Let's try it together.

00:24:11.992 --> 00:24:13.076
Ready?

00:24:13.743 --> 00:24:15.829
(Inhales)

00:24:17.164 --> 00:24:22.752
(Humming)

00:24:25.422 --> 00:24:27.340
Feel how your lips vibrate a little bit,

00:24:27.340 --> 00:24:28.758
and it kind of tickles?

00:24:29.009 --> 00:24:32.220
You can even put one hand on your belly, 
like before.

00:24:32.220 --> 00:24:34.639
And I bet it's getting smaller while
you're humming.

00:24:34.639 --> 00:24:36.057
Let's try one more time.

00:24:36.057 --> 00:24:37.392
(Inhales)

00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:41.271
(Humming)

00:24:44.941 --> 00:24:46.318
That's good.

00:24:46.318 --> 00:24:48.778
Now I love how this makes me feel.

00:24:49.154 --> 00:24:52.824
It relaxes me and it also energizes me.

00:24:53.617 --> 00:24:54.826
How does it make you feel?

00:24:54.993 --> 00:24:58.246
How does your face, and tummy, and chest
feel now?

00:24:58.705 --> 00:25:02.000
It's always important to notice
how you're feeling.

00:25:02.459 --> 00:25:05.378
Both on the inside and the outside.

00:25:06.046 --> 00:25:08.215
And if you're feeling happy
on the inside,

00:25:08.506 --> 00:25:09.883
that's wonderful.

00:25:10.425 --> 00:25:11.676
And if you're not,

00:25:12.135 --> 00:25:13.303
that's okay.

00:25:13.929 --> 00:25:16.723
But if you take a moment to breathe,

00:25:17.057 --> 00:25:20.227
it can make you feel a whole lot better.

00:25:20.477 --> 00:25:24.397
Isn't it interesting how these feelings change
when you give them time?

00:25:24.814 --> 00:25:27.609
Thank you so much for sharing
this part of your day with me.

00:25:29.027 --> 00:25:30.237
See you!

00:25:40.872 --> 00:25:42.165
Welcome back.

00:25:42.624 --> 00:25:46.753
I am so happy that you decided
to spend time with us today.

00:25:47.170 --> 00:25:49.965
And I hope you're feeling happy and excited

00:25:49.965 --> 00:25:52.467
to discover what the rest of the day brings.

00:25:52.550 --> 00:25:54.970
I'm going to try new things 
all the time now.

00:25:55.428 --> 00:25:58.056
And if you ever want to experience this again,

00:25:58.390 --> 00:25:59.557
just remember,

00:26:00.267 --> 00:26:02.310
you can take a deep breath...

00:26:02.602 --> 00:26:03.603
(Inhales)

00:26:03.603 --> 00:26:05.105
(Exhales)

00:26:05.272 --> 00:26:06.564
make some music...

00:26:08.108 --> 00:26:09.901
or notice something new.

00:26:10.652 --> 00:26:12.070
Hey! Look at this!

00:26:12.404 --> 00:26:15.782
There's much to discover in stillness.

00:26:16.741 --> 00:26:19.744
Most of all, 
stay curious about the world,

00:26:19.911 --> 00:26:23.665
and express gratitude for everything
wonderful around you.

00:26:24.499 --> 00:26:28.503
It's time to go now, 
but hopefully we see each other again soon.

00:26:28.962 --> 00:26:29.879
Goodbye!

00:26:29.879 --> 00:26:30.672
Goodbye!

00:26:30.672 --> 00:26:31.423
Bye!

00:26:31.423 --> 00:26:32.257
Bye!

00:26:32.257 --> 00:26:33.216
Bye!

00:26:33.216 --> 00:26:35.260
Thank you for letting me join you.

00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:36.761
Let's do it again.

